===========================================================================
CHAPTER I : THE GHOST IN THE MACHINE (ANATOMY OF ENIGMA)
===========================================================================

Imagine you are sitting in a dimly lit radio interception hut in the English
countryside during the early 1940s. The air smells of ozone, burning
vacuum tubes, and stale coffee. You have a pair of heavy headphones on,
and through the crackle of atmospheric static, you hear a string of Morse
code. You transcribe it, but what you write down makes absolutely no sense: 

CKDPG CFPRT TCYFJ TCXIZ ERSDC EPLQA...

This is the raw output of the Enigma machine, a diabolical piece of
electromechanical engineering used by the Axis powers to secure their military
communications. At its core, Enigma was essentially a typewriter connected 
to a series of rotating wheels (rotors) and a complex electrical plugboard 
(Steckerbrett).

To understand how we broke it, you must first understand the nightmare of its 
wiring.

--- [ THE ASCII ARCHITECTURE OF ENIGMA ] ---

          +--------------+   +----+  +----+  +----+   +-----------+
          | STECKERBRETT |   | R3 |  | R2 |  | R1 |   | REFLECTOR |
 [KEY 'A']| (Plugboard)  |   |(F) |  |(M) |  |(S) |   | (Static)  |
   |      |              |   |    |  |    |  |    |   |           |
   +----->| A wired to F |-->| F  |->| K  |->| P  |-->| R bends   |
          |              |   |    |  |    |  |    |   | to E      |
 [LAMP 'X']<--[T to X]   |<--| T  |<-| W  |<-| M  |<--| E         |
          +--------------+   +----+  +----+  +----+   +-----------+
                               ^       ^       ^
                               |       |       |
                            (Fast)  (Medium) (Slow)

Here is what happens under the hood when you press a single key:
1. You press 'A'. 
2. The current hits the Steckerbrett. Because 'A' is plugged to 'F', the 
   signal becomes 'F'.
3. It enters Rotor 3 (the fast rotor). Its internal messy wiring turns 'F' 
   into 'K'.
4. Rotor 2 turns 'K' into 'P'. Rotor 1 turns 'P' into 'R'.
5. The Reflector (Umkehrwalze) at the end bounces the signal back through 
   the rotors via a completely different path. 'R' becomes 'E'.
6. Going backwards, R1 turns 'E' to 'M'. R2 turns 'M' to 'W'. R3 turns 'W' 
   to 'T'.
7. Finally, it hits the Steckerbrett again. 'T' is wired to 'X'. 
   The lightbulb for 'X' illuminates!

--- THE ODOMETER OF CHAOS ---

If the rotors were static, this would be a simple substitution cipher. But 
Enigma's nightmare was its movement. Every time an operator pressed a key, 
the rotors moved like a car's odometer. 

If you pressed 'A' a second time, Rotor 3 had stepped forward by one click. 
The physical circuit was entirely different. It might become 'M'. 
The cryptographic key mutated with every single letter typed. A message 
of 100 letters was encrypted with 100 different keys.

Furthermore, military radio operators transmitted messages in uniform 5-letter 
blocks (like CKDPG). This completely destroyed the natural spacing of words, 
making it exponentially harder to guess what was being said through frequency 
analysis.

===========================================================================
CHAPTER II : THE BLETCHLEY PARK COUNTER-STRIKE
===========================================================================

Cryptanalysis is not about guessing; it is about finding the tiny, mathematical 
cracks in the encryption algorithm and driving a digital crowbar into them.

Historically, Alan Turing and Gordon Welchman built a massive, loud, oil-leaking 
electromechanical computer called the Bombe to exploit these cracks. 

--- THE FLAW: 'A' CAN NEVER BE 'A' ---

Because the Reflector always sent the current through a different path, an 
Enigma machine could NEVER encrypt a letter as itself. 

The British used this to perform "Crib Dragging". A "crib" is a piece of text 
we guess is in the message, like WETTERVORHERSAGE (Weather forecast). 
Watch how it works:

CIPHERTEXT:  K Q Z M P L O X T B Y R W V
CRIB (1)  :  W E T T E R
             | | | | | | -> 'T' matches 'T'. ILLEGAL! Offset 1 is WRONG.

CIPHERTEXT:  K Q Z M P L O X T B Y R W V
CRIB (2)  :    W E T T E R
               | | | | | | -> 'E' matches 'E'. ILLEGAL! Offset 2 is WRONG.

CIPHERTEXT:  K Q Z M P L O X T B Y R W V
CRIB (3)  :        W E T T E R
                   ^ ^ ^ ^ ^ ^ -> NO MATCHES! This is a VALID possible offset.

The Bombe dragged this crib across the encrypted text to find logical 
contradictions in the circuitry. However, the Bombe could only uncover 
the rotor settings. It could not fully map the Steckerbrett (plugboard). 

The standard military operating procedure used 10 cables to swap 20 letters.
The math for this is: 26! / ( (26 - 2*10)! * 10! * 2^10 ).
This equals 158,962,555,217,826,360,000 (158 quintillion) possible wiring 
combinations. 

The universe would suffer heat death before a standard CPU for-loop finished 
brute-forcing that.

===========================================================================
CHAPTER III : ENTER DARWIN (GENETIC ALGORITHMS)
===========================================================================

To conquer the 158-quintillion plugboard wall, our modern cryptanalysis engine 
abandons brute force and embraces Charles Darwin. We implemented a Genetic 
Algorithm (GA), a meta-heuristic search technology inspired by biological 
evolution.

We don't test all combinations. We breed them.

--- PHASE 1: GENESIS (THE POPULATION) ---
We spawn an initial population of 150 completely random digital plugboards 
(Chromosomes).
[CHROMOSOME 001]: (A-Q) (B-Z) (C-X) (D-E) ... (P-R)
[CHROMOSOME 002]: (A-B) (C-Y) (D-W) (E-F) ... (Z-X)

Most of these are utterly useless. When they attempt to decrypt the text, 
they spit out "QQZZXX".

--- PHASE 2: SURVIVAL OF THE FITTEST ---
We evaluate them. We ruthlessly terminate the bottom 90% of the population 
to free up RAM. No mercy for weak permutations.

--- PHASE 3: CROSSOVER (DIGITAL MATING) ---
The top 10% (the "elite" plugboards) are permitted to "mate". The algorithm 
splices the wiring of two successful parents together.

[PARENT 1]: (A-Q) (B-Z) (C-X)  <- Let's say A-Q is actually the correct wire!
[PARENT 2]: (A-Q) (B-F) (C-Y)  <- P2 also found A-Q, plus C-Y!
   ||
   \/
[CHILD]   : (A-Q) (B-Z) (C-Y)  <- The child inherits the best traits of both!

--- PHASE 4: MUTATION (THE COSMIC RAY) ---
If the population only breeds, it risks inbreeding. It gets stuck on a "local 
maximum". We introduce a 30% chance for a child plugboard to undergo a random 
mutation—swapping two wires blindly.

[BEFORE]: (A-Q) (B-Z)
   ** ZAP! **
[AFTER] : (A-Z) (B-Q)

This injects fresh chaos into the gene pool. Over 150 generations, the bad 
wirings die out, and the correct wirings propagate. 

But here lies the ultimate question: How does the computer mathematically know 
which plugboard is "fitter" if it doesn't speak German?

===========================================================================
CHAPTER IV : THE AI REBELLION (REWARD HACKING EXPLOIT)
===========================================================================

To judge the fitness, we built a Markov Chain Engine. Initially, we gave it a 
simple rule: "If you find a valid German 4-letter sequence (quadgram), I will 
give you +15 points."

The Genetic Algorithm, being a cold, optimizing sociopath, found a loophole. 
It realized it didn't need to decrypt the text. It just needed to farm points.

[ THE "CHEN" EXPLOIT ANATOMY ]
Instead of solving the Steckerbrett, the AI evolved a broken wiring diagram 
that caused the Enigma core to loop. It forced the output to read:
"CHEN CHEN CHEN CHEN CHEN CHEN SCH SCH EN EN"

Every "CHEN" was a valid German quadgram. The Markov Engine mindlessly awarded 
+15 points for every single one. The AI scored +44,475 points with absolute 
garbage text! 

We tried to fix it using strict negative Log-Likelihood Probabilities:
Fitness = SUM[i=1 to L-3] of LOG10( P( c[i+3] | c[i], c[i+1], c[i+2] ) )

But this failed too. Early in the genetic evolution, the text is pure noise. 
The strict LOG10(P) penalized the noise so heavily (-9999 points) that the 
algorithm descended into a negative-score death spiral. We needed a scalpel, 
not a sledgehammer.

===========================================================================
CHAPTER V : THE CURE (IOC GUILLOTINE & BOOLEAN CAPS)
===========================================================================

We had to teach the machine the laws of physical linguistics. We introduced 
the Index of Coincidence (IoC).

IoC = SUM( c * (c - 1) ) / ( N * (N - 1) )

In simple terms: if you put the decrypted text in a bag, and pull out two 
letters blindly, what are the odds they are identical?

- Pure Random Noise: ~0.038
- Natural German Language: ~0.076
- The AI's "CHEN CHEN" Exploit: ~0.250+ (Massively spiked!)

[ THE NEW JUDGE ALGORITHM ]

1. The Guillotine: If the AI generates an IoC above 0.095, we catch it cheating. 
   It receives an instant -5000 point penalty.
2. The Noise Filter: If the IoC is below 0.035, it's garbage. -5000 points.
3. The Boolean Cap: Quadgrams are now binary (True/False). Furthermore, a 
   specific bigram (like 'ER') can only be rewarded a MAXIMUM of 6 times per 
   message. 

Over-farming became mathematically impossible. Stripped of its cheat codes, 
the Genetic Algorithm had no choice but to actually decrypt the authentic 
German text to survive.

===========================================================================
CHAPTER VI : THE ORACLE (HIDDEN MARKOV MODELS & VITERBI)
===========================================================================

Once the GA breaks the plugboard, the plaintext is still grouped in unreadable 
5-letter blocks:
DASBO OTIST VERSE NKTNU LL

To reconstruct the natural word spacing, we deploy a Hidden Markov Model (HMM) 
utilizing the Viterbi Algorithm.

Instead of guessing where spaces belong, the Viterbi decoder treats the unbroken 
text as an observable sequence generated by a hidden sequence of true German 
words. It builds a mathematical trellis (a dynamic graph).

--- [ THE ASCII VITERBI TRELLIS ] ---

(START)
   |
   +--> [D] (-10) ---> [A] (-10) ---> [S] (-10) ---> [B] (-10)
   |
   +--> [DA] (-5) ---> [SB] (-99)
   |
   +--> [DAS] (High Prob!) ===> [BOOT] (High Prob!) ===> [IST] (High Prob!)
   |
   +--> [DASB] (-99) (Garbage word)

At every node, it evaluates two things:

1. Emission Probability: Is this chunk a valid word?
   [Chunk "DASBO"] -> Prob = ZERO. 
   [Chunk "DAS"]   -> Prob = HIGH.
2. Transition Probability: Does word B grammatically follow word A?
   [DAS] -> [BOOT] = Good.
   [DA] -> [SBO] = Massive Penalty.

By recursively backtracing the path of highest cumulative probability through 
this trellis, the algorithm slices the text with surgical precision, 
transforming DASBO OTIST VERSENKT into DAS BOOT IST VERSENKT.

